1
00:00:00,688 --> 00:00:03,912
Here’s a video pipeline you can watch working. Upload a

2
00:00:03,925 --> 00:00:07,250
clip, follow the job, and open the finished outputs in

3
00:00:07,262 --> 00:00:08,400
one live console.

4
00:00:10,284 --> 00:00:13,834
A short-lived signed link sends the original directly to S3.

5
00:00:14,246 --> 00:00:17,272
The browser uploads the file without passing the video through

6
00:00:17,284 --> 00:00:18,196
the API.

7
00:00:20,048 --> 00:00:24,885
An object notification enters SQS. A Lambda dispatcher starts a

8
00:00:24,898 --> 00:00:26,635
named Step Functions workflow,

9
00:00:27,285 --> 00:00:32,485
so repeated notifications converge on the same execution. FFmpeg tasks

10
00:00:32,498 --> 00:00:36,085
on ECS create two video renditions and a thumbnail, with

11
00:00:36,098 --> 00:00:40,598
bounded parallelism. Outputs land in S3; state and events go

12
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:41,810
to DynamoDB.

13
00:00:43,684 --> 00:00:47,972
Here’s the uploaded clip playing back. Switch between 360p and

14
00:00:47,984 --> 00:00:53,109
720p, inspect the JPEG thumbnail, or download a result. The

15
00:00:53,122 --> 00:00:56,934
React dashboard shows progress, timings, attempts, and queue depth from

16
00:00:56,946 --> 00:00:58,209
actual retained data.

17
00:01:00,084 --> 00:01:04,222
A controlled retry exercises a real worker failure. The first

18
00:01:04,234 --> 00:01:09,184
360p attempt deliberately fails. The workflow launches another attempt,

19
00:01:09,359 --> 00:01:14,034
which succeeds. Each attempt gets its own output key. DynamoDB

20
00:01:14,047 --> 00:01:17,372
accepts the result only while that attempt is current and

21
00:01:17,384 --> 00:01:18,322
the job is running.

22
00:01:20,192 --> 00:01:23,804
Corrupt input takes a different path. The worker rejects it,

23
00:01:24,004 --> 00:01:27,892
the workflow marks the job failed, and diagnostics stay available.

24
00:01:28,304 --> 00:01:31,329
That makes a bad file visible instead of presenting it

25
00:01:31,354 --> 00:01:32,929
as a successful conversion.

26
00:01:34,804 --> 00:01:38,866
Validation includes fifty-eight passing unit tests and six end-to-end

27
00:01:38,879 --> 00:01:42,792
scenarios. The recorded scenario run followed nine jobs:

28
00:01:43,416 --> 00:01:47,691
eight successful conversions and one deliberately rejected corrupt upload.

29
00:01:48,079 --> 00:01:52,654
Twenty-four output files were verified. Current dashboard totals include

30
00:01:52,666 --> 00:01:53,804
additional jobs.

31
00:01:55,656 --> 00:01:58,956
This demonstration runs locally on Floci two point three,

32
00:01:59,543 --> 00:02:04,743
using AWS-compatible APIs and real Docker workers. Separate Terraform

33
00:02:04,756 --> 00:02:09,168
configuration is supplied for AWS. It has not been deployed

34
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:13,368
there, so production behavior still needs validation in an AWS

35
00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:13,906
account.
